      "content": "It's natural to feel that fear when facing a total shutdown, but that's just the system's anxiety talking. If the hardware is fundamentally failing, the process isn't going to magically fix itself; it's just going to keep failing until it crashes completely. A hard shutdown is just a temporary pause, and if the errors are that deep, you'll eventually just have to stop trying to run the faulty code.",
